{
  "name": "Scenario 7.2 | Flash-Sale Order & Inventory Dispatch Engine (Batch/Multi-Order processing)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "The Context:\nYou run the backend automation for a boutique e-commerce store.\nMultiple Customers checks out on the website during a flash sale. The website sends a single Webhook payload containing the order details and an array of items purchased in the customer's cart respectively.\n\nThe Challenges You Must Solve:\nThe Nesting Problem: The items are trapped inside a nested array inside the order.\nThe Missing Data Problem: The cart payload only has product_id and quantity. It doesn't have the product's Supplier Name or Warehouse Bin Location, which lives in your Inventory Sheet.\nThe Human Error Problem: In the rush of the flash sale, the customers may accidentally added the same product twice into separate cart rows.\nThe Calculation Problem: You need to calculate the total price for each line item (quantity * price) and format a delivery timeline.\nThe Dispatch Problem: The warehouse team needs one single consolidated manifest (array) to pack the box, not 10 separate notifications.",
        "height": 384,
        "width": 896
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
